+# Working in this repo with Rojo
+
+Git is the source of truth. The files under `src/` are the game; your Studio dev place is a build
+of them that `rojo serve` keeps up to date. `README.md`'s Layout table says which folder becomes
+which instance.
+
+## First-time setup
+
+1. Install the tools: `rokit install` (versions are pinned in `rokit.toml`).
+2. Install packages: `pesde install` in the repo root, then again in `test_packages/` for Jest.
+   Both install folders (`roblox_packages/`) are generated and ignored by Git.
+3. Make your own dev place: publish a fresh Baseplate to your own account or group, and use only
+   that place for `rojo serve`. Never connect to a shared or live place.
+4. Optional but recommended: add your dev place's id to `servePlaceIds` in your local copy of
+   `default.project.json`, so Rojo refuses to live-sync into any other place. Don't commit your
+   own id unless the team has agreed to keep a shared list there.
+
+## Day to day
+
+1. Pull, and if `pesde.toml`, `pesde.lock`, or `test_packages/pesde.*` changed, rerun
+   `pesde install` (with `rojo serve` stopped).
+2. Start `rojo serve` in the repo root (port 34872), open your dev place, and click **Connect**
+   in the Rojo plugin.
+3. Make every change in files, in your editor. Studio is for reading, running specs, and
+   playtesting.
+4. Before you push, run the checks from the README (`rojo sourcemap`, `luau-lsp analyze`,
+   `selene src`, `stylua --check src`) and run the Jest specs in your dev place.
+5. Commit on your own branch, and check `git status` shows only the files you meant to change.
+
+### Where changes go
+
+| You want | Put it in |
+|---|---|
+| Server code | `src/ServerScriptService` (`*.server.luau` for Scripts) |
+| Code shared by server and client | `src/ReplicatedStorage/Shared` |
+| Client code | `src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts` (`*.client.luau` for LocalScripts) |
+| UI | `src/StarterGui` |
+| A Jest spec | `src/ServerScriptService/Tests/Specs/<Name>.spec.luau` |
+| A package | `pesde.toml` (game) or `test_packages/pesde.toml` (test-only), then `pesde install` |
+
+Don't edit scripts, properties, attributes, or tags in Studio under a synced folder: the next
+sync overwrites the edit, and Git never sees it. Never edit files in `roblox_packages/`: pesde
+replaces them on every install, and they are hardlinked into other projects.
+
+## While serving, check
+
+- **Your edit arrived.** Open the script in Studio and confirm the new text is there before you
+  run a spec or playtest. If an error's line number doesn't move with your edit, Studio is
+  still running the old code.
+- **`rojo serve` is still running after you delete, move, or rename a file or folder.** Rojo
+  7.7.0 and 7.7.1 can crash on these (`Rojo crashed!` in the terminal), and Studio then silently
+  stops receiving changes. Restart `rojo serve` and click Connect again.
+- **You're on the branch you think you are.** The place runs whatever is checked out in the
+  folder `rojo serve` started in. Stop the server before `git checkout`, `pull`, `rebase`,
+  `stash`, `reset`, or `pesde install`, and start it again afterward.
+- **The place looks right:** `ServerScriptService.Tests` holds `Specs` and `Packages` (Jest), and
+  `ReplicatedStorage.Packages` holds the game packages.
+
+## Don't break default.project.json
+
+The project file decides where everything lands, so a small mistake moves or drops whole
+folders (for example, Jest no longer finds `ServerScriptService.Tests.Packages`).
+
+- **Change it only when the layout really changes,** and update `README.md`'s Layout table in
+  the same commit. The table and the project file must agree.
+- **Keep `globIgnorePaths`.** `src/ServerScriptService/Tests` is mounted on its own node so the
+  test packages can sit inside it, and the ignore entry stops the `ServerScriptService` mount
+  from adding a second `Tests` folder.
+- **Resolving a merge conflict in it:** don't just pick one side. Keep every mount from both
+  sides, check each `$path` against the real folder names (`StarterPlayerScripts` has an `s`),
+  and compare the result with the README's Layout table.
+- **Save it as UTF-8 without a BOM.** Rojo can't parse a project file that starts with a byte
+  order mark. Windows PowerShell 5.1's `Set-Content` and `Out-File` add one, and some editors and
+  merge tools do too. Check with `head -c 3 default.project.json | od -An -tx1`; `ef bb bf` means
+  it has a BOM.
+- **Verify before you push:**
+  `rojo sourcemap default.project.json -o sourcemap.json --include-non-scripts` must succeed,
+  and `sourcemap.json` should show `Tests` > `Packages` > `Jest` under `ServerScriptService`. Then
+  restart `rojo serve`, reconnect, and run the specs once.
